From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] regulator: Add support for MediaTek MT6368 SPMI PMIC Regulators

Add a driver for the regulators of the MediaTek MT6368 SPMI PMIC, based
on the MT6363 one: the regulators are a child of the PMIC, with their own
regmap at the base the device tree gives, and their overcurrent
interrupts come from the PMIC interrupt controller of the mtk-spmi-pmic
MFD driver.

Unlike the MT6363 driver, the regmap has 8-bit values, as the registers
have: with 16-bit values every write would also write the next register,
which here is a CLR register after a SET register, or the next enable
register after a CLR register. The MT6368 has no hardware voted low power
mode and no operating mode registers, so the mode comes from the low
power bit and there is no set_load. As on the MT6373, VMCH can be
switched by an external interrupt, and the shutdown enables the power
off sequence of the PMIC.

Also address the review of the MT6373 driver: regmap_bulk_write() takes
a number of registers, an overcurrent interrupt is always reported, and
the work that enables the interrupt again is cancelled with the
regulator.

The registers, less the 0x30 base of the regulators node, the voltage
tables and the interrupt numbers are those of the MediaTek MT6368 driver
in the OnePlus MT6897 kernel (OnePlusOSS
android_kernel_modules_and_devicetree_oneplus_mt6897, branch
oneplus/mt6897_b_16.0.0_oneplus_pad). As in the MT6363 driver, VOCAL adds
up to ten 10mV steps to the voltage that VOSEL picks.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/agKKuH0fP3lBMuFd@sirena.co.uk

---
 drivers/regulator/Kconfig                  |  11 +
 drivers/regulator/Makefile                 |   1 +
 drivers/regulator/mt6368-regulator.c       | 683 +++++++++++++++++++++
 include/linux/regulator/mt6368-regulator.h | 113 ++++
 4 files changed, 808 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/regulator/Kconfig b/drivers/regulator/Kconfig
index a54a549..b48f954 100644
--- a/drivers/regulator/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/regulator/Kconfig
@@ -984,6 +984,17 @@ config REGULATOR_MT6363
 	  This driver supports the control of different power rails of device
 	  through regulator interface.
 
+config REGULATOR_MT6368
+	tristate "MT6368 SPMI PMIC regulator driver"
+	depends on SPMI
+	select REGMAP_SPMI
+	select IRQ_DOMAIN
+	help
+	  Say Y here to enable support for regulators found in the MediaTek
+	  MT6368 SPMI PMIC.
+	  This driver supports the control of different power rails of device
+	  through regulator interface.
+
